From 9dbb70bc019833abe47c234f1011f2911a12a240 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:57:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: overlay the unlock prompt on the running
 screensaver

While a session is locked the frame-source screensaver is shown on the
lock surface, but on the first input the lock discarded it and painted
the prompt over a flat background, so the saver vanished the moment the
user touched the machine.

Keep the frame source running for as long as the lock is held instead of
stopping it on input. The lock client now holds a read-only view of the
current frame and, when the prompt is raised, composites the clock and
password card over that frame behind a light scrim; after the prompt has
been idle the raw frames show again. The frame source is never stopped
for input, and it hands the host the frame's pixels alongside the
wl_buffer so a host can composite without a second copy.

Failure containment is unchanged: a stopped or crashed source clears the
frame and the prompt falls back to the lock's own dark background while
the session stays locked. The feature stays behind -Dlock_framesrc
(default off) and inert unless a renderer is configured.

The headless labwc test now checks that input raises the prompt without
stopping the source, that frames keep streaming behind it, that a real
screen capture shows the backdrop is not the flat fill, and that the
prompt returns to the frames after it has been idle.
